Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• HISTORY_NODES."id": unique identifier of each historical node; needed for joining with PLANET_NODES to see if a node still exists.  
• HISTORY_NODES."username": author of each historical edit; this is the field we eventually have to rank.  
• HISTORY_NODES."latitude", HISTORY_NODES."longitude": coordinates that let us keep only nodes inside the requested rectangle.  
• HISTORY_NODES."all_tags": JSON array that can contain {"key":"amenity","value":"hospital|clinic|doctors"}; used to detect medical‑amenity nodes.  
• PLANET_NODES."id": current node identifiers; used to exclude historical nodes that are still present.  
• PLANET_NODES."all_tags": optional check whether the node is still a medical amenity.  
• PLANET_NODES."latitude", PLANET_NODES."longitude": can be used to double‑check current positions if needed.  

Typical conditions that will be applied  

• Bounding box  
  CAST("latitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921  
  AND CAST("longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246  

• Medical amenity filter (on a flattened tag)  
  f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'  
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('hospital','clinic','doctors')  

• Dropped‑node filter  
  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1  
               FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p  
               WHERE p."id" = h."id")  


Ten progressive Snowflake SQLs (each shows up to 20 rows)  

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a few historical nodes inside the rectangle, no tag filter yet
SELECT h."id",
       h."username",
       h."latitude",
       h."longitude",
       h."all_tags"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h
WHERE  CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND  CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Inspect the structure of the all_tags JSON to understand its keys
SELECT f.value
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.SEQ < 20          -- only the first 20 flattened elements
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) List distinct amenity values that appear in the rectangle (historical data)
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"value"::STRING AS amenity
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
WHERE  CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND  CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND  f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Pull historical nodes in the rectangle that are tagged hospital / clinic / doctors
SELECT h."id",
       h."username",
       h."all_tags"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
WHERE  CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND  CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND  f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND  f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('hospital','clinic','doctors')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Count historical medical nodes per username inside rectangle (ignoring whether they still exist)
SELECT   h."username",
         COUNT(*) AS hist_medical_nodes
FROM     "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
WHERE    CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND    CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND    f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND    f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('hospital','clinic','doctors')
GROUP BY h."username"
ORDER BY hist_medical_nodes DESC
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Show medical amenity nodes that still exist in current planet_nodes (sanity check)
SELECT h."id",
       h."username",
       h."latitude",
       h."longitude"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES"  h
JOIN   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES"   p
           ON p."id" = h."id"
JOIN   LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
           ON TRUE
WHERE  CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND  CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND  f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND  f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('hospital','clinic','doctors')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Historical medical amenity nodes that are NOT in current planet_nodes
SELECT h."id",
       h."username",
       h."latitude",
       h."longitude"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" h
JOIN   LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => h."all_tags") f
           ON TRUE
WHERE  CAST(h."latitude"  AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND  CAST(h."longitude" AS FLOAT) BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND  f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND  f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('hospital','clinic','doctors')
  AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                   FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p
                   WHERE p."id" = h."id")
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Quick inspection of one username’s dropped medical nodes (replace 'some_user' if desired)
